<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>智能新闻| smithsonianmag.com</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/rss/smart-news/</link><description>智能新闻的 RSS 提要</description><lastBuildDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 02:04:11 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>美国宇航局南希·格雷斯·罗马太空望远镜发射寻找系外行星并解开暗物质和暗能量之谜</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/nasas-nancy-grace-roman-space-telescope-launches-to-find-exoplanets-and-unravel-mysteries-of-dark-matter-and-dark-energy-180989268/</link><description>新天文台将在五年内完成三项宇宙调查，尽管它的设计运行时间至少是原来的两倍。它的数据可能会改变科学家对宇宙的基本理解</description><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 11:26:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/nasas-nancy-grace-roman-space-telescope-launches-to-find-exoplanets-and-unravel-mysteries-of-dark-matter-and-dark-energy-180989268/</guid></item><item><title>森林在古代全球变暖事件中表现不佳，为当今的气候变化提供了一个“警示”故事</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/forests-didnt-fare-well-during-an-ancient-global-warming-event-offering-a-cautionary-tale-about-todays-climate-change-180989353/</link><description>一项研究表明，5600 万年前的一场剧烈的全球变暖事件导致现代怀俄明州的森林失去了约 60% 的树冠覆盖率，并且花了 10 万多年的时间才恢复过来</description><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 18:43:58 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/forests-didnt-fare-well-during-an-ancient-global-warming-event-offering-a-cautionary-tale-about-todays-climate-change-180989353/</guid></item><item><title>在西班牙洞穴深处，罗马妇女可能崇拜一位神秘的女神</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/deep-inside-spanish-cave-roman-women-may-have-worshipped-mysterious-goddess-180989414/</link><description>瓦伦西亚的科瓦德莱多内斯 (Cova de les Dones) 以其旧石器时代艺术而闻名，这里还拥有一座罗马圣所，研究人员称，那里的女性似乎在崇拜女性神的过程中发挥了积极作用</description><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 18:43:43 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/deep-inside-spanish-cave-roman-women-may-have-worshipped-mysterious-goddess-180989414/</guid></item><item><title>研究表明，历史污染，而不是当前的工业排放，损害了世界上最大、最古老的古代岩石艺术收藏</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/historical-pollution-not-current-industrial-emissions-damaged-worlds-largest-oldest-collection-ancient-rock-art-180989416/</link><description>研究人员表示，过去接触二氧化硫可能是恩加达-恩加利人数万年前创造的穆鲁朱加岩画孔隙度增加的原因</description><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 18:04:36 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/historical-pollution-not-current-industrial-emissions-damaged-worlds-largest-oldest-collection-ancient-rock-art-180989416/</guid></item><item><title>这颗恒星以破纪录的速度绕我们银河系的中心运行，可能有助于揭开有关那里巨大黑洞的秘密</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-star-orbits-our-galaxys-heart-at-a-record-breaking-speed-and-could-help-uncover-secrets-about-the-behemoth-black-hole-there-180989393/</link><description>Speedster 的行驶速度高达每小时 5600 万英里，约为光速的 8%。它还非常接近银河系中心的超大质量黑洞</description><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 15:45:08 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-star-orbits-our-galaxys-heart-at-a-record-breaking-speed-and-could-help-uncover-secrets-about-the-behemoth-black-hole-there-180989393/</guid></item><item><title>一位房东在一间空置的公寓里发现了一幅奇怪的印刷品。原来是失踪八年的毕加索原作</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-landlord-found-a-peculiar-print-hanging-in-a-vacant-apartment-it-turned-out-to-be-an-original-picasso-print-that-had-been-missing-for-eight-years-180989417/</link><description>2018 年，当“斗牛士”从密尔沃基一家美术馆消失时，店主不知道是否还能再次看到它。发现这幅蚀刻画的男子本月早些时候将其交给了警方</description><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 15:37:31 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-landlord-found-a-peculiar-print-hanging-in-a-vacant-apartment-it-turned-out-to-be-an-original-picasso-print-that-had-been-missing-for-eight-years-180989417/</guid></item><item><title>当水果稀缺时，这些猴子就会捕食动物。这种行为可能为人类食肉习惯的起源提供线索</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/when-fruit-is-scarce-these-monkeys-hunt-animals-the-behavior-may-offer-clues-about-the-origins-of-humans-meat-eating-habits-180989412/</link><description>巴西东北部的胡须卷尾猴通常吃植物性食物，但当这些来源有限时，它们就会转向小型脊椎动物。我们的祖先可能也做了同样的事，最终让掠夺行为在我们的血统中更频繁地传承下去</description><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/when-fruit-is-scarce-these-monkeys-hunt-animals-the-behavior-may-offer-clues-about-the-origins-of-humans-meat-eating-habits-180989412/</guid></item><item><title>蜗牛可以根据自己的需要使粘液变得粘稠、滑滑、泡沫状或坚硬。这是他们如何调整多用途粘液的方法</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/snails-can-make-their-slime-sticky-slippery-foamy-or-hard-depending-on-their-needs-heres-how-they-tweak-their-multipurpose-mucus-180989361/</link><description>这些生物可以改变多功能物质中钙和胶原蛋白的比例，从而改变蛋白质结构。不同的纹理可以帮助蜗牛滑行、攀爬或保护自己</description><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 20:04:47 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/snails-can-make-their-slime-sticky-slippery-foamy-or-hard-depending-on-their-needs-heres-how-they-tweak-their-multipurpose-mucus-180989361/</guid></item><item><title>经过十年的修复工作，1,800 名志愿者将一座 400 吨重的日本城堡拉回原位</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/1800-people-pull-a-400-ton-japanese-castle-keep-back-toward-its-original-location-after-a-decade-of-restoration-work-180989401/</link><description>帮助移动城堡的机会吸引了来自日本和国外的数千份申请。成群结队的彩票中奖者轮流拉动连接在巨大结构上的粗绳子</description><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 19:43:03 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/1800-people-pull-a-400-ton-japanese-castle-keep-back-toward-its-original-location-after-a-decade-of-restoration-work-180989401/</guid></item><item><title>梅尔·布鲁克斯最喜欢的电影是什么？为了庆祝他的 100 岁生日，这位喜剧传奇人物挑选了 20 部影片在洛杉矶放映</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/what-are-mel-brooks-favorite-movies-to-celebrate-100th-birthday-comedy-legend-picks-20-films-to-screen-across-los-angeles-180989410/</link><description>不拘一格的节目跨越数十年和流派，让人们一睹布鲁克斯的喜剧影响、个人历史和对电影的持久热爱</description><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 19:23:15 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/what-are-mel-brooks-favorite-movies-to-celebrate-100th-birthday-comedy-legend-picks-20-films-to-screen-across-los-angeles-180989410/</guid></item><item><title>阿拉巴马州一家与民权运动有关的历史悠久的酒店正在倒塌。为拯救它而奋斗的环保主义者能否扭转局势？</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/historic-alabama-hotel-linked-civil-rights-movement-is-falling-apart-can-conservationists-fighting-to-save-it-turn-the-tide-180989407/</link><description>塞尔玛的埃迪斯通酒店见证了从重建到“血腥星期日”的美国历史的关键篇章。现在，经过多年的忽视和最近的围墙倒塌，保护基金正在努力确保其未来</description><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 18:35:02 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/historic-alabama-hotel-linked-civil-rights-movement-is-falling-apart-can-conservationists-fighting-to-save-it-turn-the-tide-180989407/</guid></item><item><title>为什么这位 17 世纪波兰妇女的脚趾上挂着挂锁，脖子上挂着一把铁镰刀？</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/why-was-this-17th-century-polish-woman-buried-with-a-padlock-on-her-toe-and-an-iron-sickle-across-her-neck-180989408/</link><description>新的研究表明，埋葬这名年轻女子的人采取了预防措施，以阻止她复活并对他们进行报复</description><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 17:51:52 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/why-was-this-17th-century-polish-woman-buried-with-a-padlock-on-her-toe-and-an-iron-sickle-across-her-neck-180989408/</guid></item><item><title>古生物学家在拉布雷亚焦油坑发现了一种新的冰河时代蟾蜍，为该地区古代气候提供了线索</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/paleontologists-discover-a-new-species-of-ice-age-toad-at-the-la-brea-tar-pits-offering-clues-about-the-areas-ancient-climate-180989390/</link><description>这些化石遗骸于 1929 年被发现，是拉布雷亚研究相对较少的两栖动物收藏的一部分。由于蟾蜍是冷血动物并且对环境变化敏感，这一发现可以帮助研究人员拼凑出过去的气候条件</description><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 15:37:27 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/paleontologists-discover-a-new-species-of-ice-age-toad-at-the-la-brea-tar-pits-offering-clues-about-the-areas-ancient-climate-180989390/</guid></item><item><title>Freddie Mercury 突破界限的服装成为维多利亚和阿尔伯特博物馆的焦点，纪念他诞辰 80 周年</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/freddie-mercurys-boundary-pushing-costumes-take-center-stage-at-victoria-and-albert-museum-to-mark-80th-anniversary-his-birth-180989403/</link><description>这位女王主唱职业生涯中的八件套装将在伦敦博物馆的永久画廊的六站中展出，让人们一睹他传奇舞台形象背后的服装</description><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 14:34:47 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/freddie-mercurys-boundary-pushing-costumes-take-center-stage-at-victoria-and-albert-museum-to-mark-80th-anniversary-his-birth-180989403/</guid></item><item><title>研究表明，2016 年至 2021 年间去世的前 NFL 球员中至少有四分之一患有进行性脑部疾病 CTE</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/at-least-one-in-four-former-nfl-players-who-died-between-2016-and-2021-had-the-progressive-brain-disease-cte-study-suggests-180989406/</link><description>在已故足球运动员中，神经退行性疾病（与反复头部受伤有关）的真实患病率可能要高得多。 CTE 也会影响其他运动员，包括曲棍球运动员、足球运动员和摔跤运动员</description><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/at-least-one-in-four-former-nfl-players-who-died-between-2016-and-2021-had-the-progressive-brain-disease-cte-study-suggests-180989406/</guid></item><item><title>卢浮宫精选伊斯兰杰作首次来到美国。参观即将在史密森国家亚洲艺术博物馆展出的珍品</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/for-the-first-time-a-selection-of-islamic-masterpieces-from-the-louvre-is-coming-to-the-united-states-see-the-treasures-soon-to-be-displayed-at-the-smithsonians-national-museum-of-asian-art-180989402/</link><description>九月的展览将展出跨越多个世纪和地区的 26 件作品，题为“来自卢浮宫：伊斯兰艺术杰作”</description><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 19:00:22 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/for-the-first-time-a-selection-of-islamic-masterpieces-from-the-louvre-is-coming-to-the-united-states-see-the-treasures-soon-to-be-displayed-at-the-smithsonians-national-museum-of-asian-art-180989402/</guid></item><item><title>本周将目光转向夜空，观看近乎全食的月食。它会暂时把月亮变成红色</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/turn-your-eyes-to-the-night-skies-this-week-to-see-a-near-total-lunar-eclipse-itll-temporarily-turn-the-moon-red-180989404/</link><description>在高峰期，月球 96% 的面积将位于地球阴影最暗的部分内。由于阳光穿过地球大气层，该球体将呈现出怪异的光芒</description><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 18:57:29 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/turn-your-eyes-to-the-night-skies-this-week-to-see-a-near-total-lunar-eclipse-itll-temporarily-turn-the-moon-red-180989404/</guid></item><item><title>2200 年前的罗马沉船残骸上的易碎涂层揭示了古代水手如何使船只保持漂浮</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/brittle-coating-on-2200-year-old-roman-shipwreck-revealing-how-ancient-soliders-kept-ships-afloat-180989394/</link><description>船上保存的松焦油和蜂蜡的痕迹揭示了几千年前造船厂用来保护船只免受深海侵蚀的艰苦技术</description><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 18:45:17 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/brittle-coating-on-2200-year-old-roman-shipwreck-revealing-how-ancient-soliders-kept-ships-afloat-180989394/</guid></item><item><title>查看年度野生动物摄影师奖中的 16 张令人惊叹的动物照片</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-16-stunning-animal-images-from-the-wildlife-photographer-of-the-year-awards-180989397/</link><description>这项著名的比赛现已进入第 62 个年头，在 10 月份宣布获奖者之前，先睹为快地公布了本次比赛的参赛作品</description><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 18:28:04 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-16-stunning-animal-images-from-the-wildlife-photographer-of-the-year-awards-180989397/</guid></item><item><title>这些中世纪手稿碎片被重新用作羊皮纸，无意中将它们保存了几个世纪</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-medieval-manuscript-fragments-were-reused-as-parchment-inadvertently-preserving-them-for-centuries-180989398/</link><description>最近在海峡群岛之一根西岛发现的这些书页包括圣经段落、诗歌、戏剧和其他文本。它们在 16 世纪和 17 世纪被重新用作书籍装订</description><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 18:20:50 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/these-medieval-manuscript-fragments-were-reused-as-parchment-inadvertently-preserving-them-for-centuries-180989398/</guid></item></channel></rss>